{
  "raw": {
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Graduate-Admissions-Counselor_R0007942": {
      "title": "Graduate Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe Graduate Admissions Counselor is responsible for developing and maintaining a positive relationship with graduate applicants (both domestic and international) at all levels and during all phases of the recruiting and application process. This position serves as the primary contact for all graduate inquiries and applicants and engages in comprehensive recruiting and conversion work. This individual is also responsible for working within the university environment to facilitate enrollment and effective working relations among schools/departments as assigned. This position is In-Person Essential functions Work toward and achieve the college/school/program’s enrollment goals by participating in the recruitment activities that include: Providing information to prospective students regarding graduate programs, admission requirements, and required documents. Preparing presentations for prospective and accepted student audiences both small and large, as required. Coordinating and participating in on-campus events for prospects, accepted students, and special interest groups, as required. Traveling where designated to represent the University and supporting recruiting efforts. This includes individual college/university visits, college fairs, conferences, and off-campus events. Conducting various mail, text, phone, and email recruiting campaigns to generate inquiries and applications using the CRM system Responding by phone, text, email, and/or mail to all inquiries received and tracking them using the CRM system. Conducting information sessions and attending college fairs and other events. Counseling prospective students to encourage campus visits and application submission utilizing the CRM system. Managing campus visits and scheduling prospective students, including meeting with faculty. Represent the Barry University brand and serve as a content expert for prospective students and others for the program for which the Graduate Admissions Counselor is responsible. Execute additional tactics that support strategies established by the Deans and AVP to attract, recruit, and enroll qualified students to the program. Assist the Senior Director in assessing results of prior recruitment travel and development of subsequent recruitment travel. Facilitate timely and appropriate information delivery to move students through the various stages from inquiry to applicant and support the conversion of applicants to accepted and enrolled students Determine the prospective student's preferred method of communication, incorporating all media types to ensure the transmission of information is complete, succinct, and anticipatory in nature. Create and conduct follow-up via phone, live chat, web, text, and other methods of communication with prospects and applicants with appropriate tracking using the CRM system. Explain admission requirements for specific programs such as standardized test requirements, test waivers, essays, format for recommendation letters, transcript requirements, scholarships, discounts, and resources available to assist prospective students with the process. Advise and guide prospective students, as appropriate, throughout the application and decision-making process, providing high-level coaching as well as technical assistance throughout the relationship utilizing the CRM system. Promote prospect/applicant engagement with peers, faculty, and staff including department liaisons and academic advisors. Develop and maintain expertise in describing the university’s financial aid opportunities and awarding policies and practices and ensure the highest level of service and accuracy. Document all contact with applicants in Salesforce, the university’s customer relationship management (CRM) tool. Report daily, weekly, and monthly activities utilizing CRM systems. Conduct regular assessment of interactions with prospective students and make recommendations for needed updates of information to improve the customer experience and tracking in the CRM system. Maintain effective communications with the departments of Financial Aid, Graduate Admissions and with the various academic programs/schools as necessary to facilitate their efforts in the application and conversion process. Assist with the onboarding and registration process by instructing students on the steps toward advising and registration, and assisting with holds/restrictions and explaining why hold restrictions cannot be overridden. Facilitate daily business in conducting Graduate Admissions work by: Maintaining a professional appearance at all times and conducting yourself in a professional manner while holding true to the core values of Barry University. Demonstrating and possessing a strong understanding of cultural competency and how to communicate to different audiences. Representing the University brand with the highest level of integrity. Safeguarding the confidentiality of student, staff, and university information by exercising discretion in managing records and communication with faculty, staff, alumni, and prospective students. Making recommendations for process improvements to improve workflow. Evaluating readiness of applicants’ files upon receipt of each new credential to be sent to the Program Director for review and decision. Collect, synthesize, and analyze data using the CRM system for the following purposes: Prepare weekly/monthly reports on recruitment activities Utilize data to provide monthly assessments of progress toward identified objectives and goals. Provide support for monthly assessments of progress toward identified objectives and goals. Provide support to the Senior Director in the creation of the recruitment strategy and take responsibility for executing the plan of action. Perform other job-related duties as assigned or required for the position. Qualifications/Requirements A Bachelor's degree in any discipline is required. 1-3 years of relevant experience is required. Intermediate experience with MS Office Suite. Experience with Colleague is preferred. Must possess excellent interpersonal and cross-cultural communication skills, with the ability to actively listen, build positive relationships, and effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Orlando--Law-Campus/Evening-Circulation-Assistant_R0007907": {
      "title": "Evening Circulation Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe top priority of the Circulation Assistant is to provide prompt, knowledgeable, and efficient service to the Law Library's patrons as part of the Public Services team. The Assistant fills one of the primary front line customer service positions and is essential to the proper functioning of the Law Library. The standard hours of this position are Sunday through Thursday, 1:00 p.m. to 10:00 p.m. while school is in session and from 3:00 p.m. to midnight during final exams. During Intersession, the Evening Circulation Assistant will be required to work a Monday through Friday schedule during library operating hours. 1.          Closes Law Library: Performs shutdown duties, including shutting down equipment, clearing off tables, shelving carts, and other tasks Works with the security guards in closing Library and alerting them to any security issues. 2.          Acts as the Law Library's primary point of contact for responding to unforeseen and/or exigent circumstances after 5:00 PM Assesses the situation If necessary, determines and contacts the appropriate authority 3.          Assists patrons at the Circulation Desk, including: Enforces Library policies, including Library admittance policies Serves as Library's face-to-face point of contact with evening f acuity Advises patrons of circulation policies, providing requested reserve materials Answers directional and location reference questions Checks Library materials in and out Answers all other questions or directs patron to the proper person or resource to provide answer Could be asked to be trained/certified as a Notary to assist with evening requests, if needed. Assists patrons in making study room reservations Assists patrons by sending faxes 4.          Acts as evening technology point person within the library: Instructs patrons in the use of the library’s printer/copiers, PrintMe wireless printing service, computers and Wi-Fi Replaces paper and toner in copiers Removes paper jams Notifies repair service when more serious problems exist Uses Helpdesk to inform DolT if computers are not working or of other technology or equipment issues Contacts outside technology maintenance company when appropriate 5.          Helps to maintain the library’s order: Using Library of Congress call number system, shelves books left on tables and book carts Using Library of Congress call number system, shelf reads/shifts collection, as needed Maintains neat appearance of the library, including study tables, carrels, and study rooms Assists with shifting the stacks when space is needed Contacts campus facilities as needed 6.          Statistics, data entry and filing: Tracks evening Library patron and usage statistics At the direction of the Access Services Librarian/Circulation Supervisor, compiles, collects, and reports department statistics. 7           Works with student assistants: At the direction of the Access Services Librarian/Circulation Supervisor, assists with the supervision of student workers At the direction of the Access Services Librarian/Circulation Supervisor, assists with the training of student workers 8. Acts as a backup for processing interlibrary loan requests as needed. Maintains familiarity with ILL processes by regularly processing incoming and outgoing requests. 9. Performs other related duties as assigned or as required. This position primarily maintains an evening/weekend working schedule, but the schedule is subject to change when needed. At times serves as the only full-time employee on campus. The position holder must be service oriented, with a thorough knowledge of the Law Library's circulation policies and the location of materials in the library; must place customer service as a top priority and must have a helpful attitude and demeanor. As the only full-time non-student Law Library staff member during a large portion of the shift, this is a key position in the Law Library. Without a com patent person in this position, the Law Library cannot operate for the necessary hours required for accreditation. Qualifications/Requirements: Associates Degree required.  Bachelor’s degree preferred. An equivalent combination of education and progressively responsible related experience may be considered in lieu of the degree requirement. 1-3 years previous experience. Excellent written and oral communication skills required. Ability to learn and perform basic maintenance functions for copiers, computers and printers within the library. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Math-Lab-Tutor_R0007929": {
      "title": "Math Lab Tutor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nSummary The part-time Math Lab tutor tutors a diverse population of undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students in the Math Lab. The tutor works in the Math Lab for approximately 10-15 hours per week, Mondays through Saturdays. Essential Functions Provides one-on-one and small-group tutorial services to a diverse population of undergraduate students.  The tutor Identifies students’ mathematical skills needs; Differentiates strategies and instructional materials to meet individual students’ needs; Teach students specific math concepts; Engages students in tutoring sessions by utilizing active learning strategies; Fosters student autonomy, as developmentally appropriate; Motivates students by being an active listener; and Respects students’ diverse backgrounds and unique perspectives Documents student work and progress by: Using the processes and systems established within the Math Lab to document student progress; Entering all data in a timely fashion as specified by the Manager, Glenn Hubert Learning Center and Testing Center; and Communicating with the Manager, Glenn Hubert Learning Center and Testing Center regarding students with challenging or unique situations and documenting record details of such situations through the specified means within the Math Lab. Participates in professional development and training sessions as related to tutor responsibilities. The tutor: Maintains currency in the content area (e.g. researches and develops new and varied instructional materials and strategies); Actively participates in learning community meetings; Participates in departmental professional development sessions and staff meetings throughout the semester; Serves as a proctor for student placement testing; Maintains currency with technological resources for instructional and recordkeeping purposes; and Monitors and arranges for replenishment of consumable materials used in the tutoring environment. Qualifications/Requirements A Bachelor's degree in Mathematics, Mathematics Education is required. A Master's degree is preferred. 3-5 years of teaching experience is required. Must have intermediate experience with Microsoft applications for communication, reporting, and analyzing data and other information.    Be able to learn to use other software tools independently. Experience using Scantron and other office equipment. Must be able to s peak and write professionally to communicate data results to students, parents, faculty, and/or staff.   Prepare reports for a variety of audiences. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/HVAC-Mechanic_R0007612": {
      "title": "HVAC Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nSummary The HVAC Mechanic works under the supervision of the Maintenance Manager. Performs routine preventive maintenance on HVAC equipment and also HVAC layout, construction, modification, testing, adjustment, and calibration of HVAC equipment. Must be able and available to be on-call after hours and/or weekends. Essential Functions Performs tasks by using the standard power tools, materials, and trade codes Able to schedule, start, stop equipment, and adjust parameters to the HVAC system utilizing the energy management system. Ability to read and understand blueprints and be able to communicate verbally and in writing with fellow employees Perform other related duties incidental to the needs of the department Maintains, troubleshoot, repair, and clean: cooling towers, air compressors, air handlers, exhaust, supply fans, water pumps, direct expansion equipment, refrigeration units, and other related equipment. Keep all areas organized. Must be able to research and order HVAC equipment and supplies. Knowledge of the methods, materials, tools, and practices used in the HVAC trade Follow all proper safety procedures and use proper PPE. Must follow all OSHA guidelines as to equipment and materials used. Possesses a sound working knowledge of HVAC, including the concepts of voltage, current, and power, and the properties and uses of electrical components, including resistors, inductors, capacitors, relays, contactors, and transformers. Must be able to follow all proper procedures on Schooldude. Qualifications/Requirements High school diploma or GED required. Training certification for HVAC including chillers. The candidate must be able to handle multiple tasks, prioritize, and coordinate work assignments with other trades. 3-5 years of proven experience in a similar or the same position. Must be able to identify recurring maintenance problems and make appropriate recommendations. Must have experience using a two-way radio, phone, Personal Digital Assistant, power-driven, and manually operated equipment tools. The candidate must be able to communicate in English. This position requires the ability to lift, bend, stoop, climb, and reach. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Orlando--Law-Campus/Manager--Recruitment---Employer-Relations_R0007909": {
      "title": "Manager, Recruitment & Employer Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nThe Manager, Recruitment & Employer Relations supports the strategic and operational delivery of Career Services, with primary responsibility for employer engagement and recruitment initiatives, career counseling for assigned students, and pro bono/community service program administration. The Manager identifies employer contacts, employment and experiential opportunities for students and alumni, and coordinates recruitment programs including On Campus Interviews and resume collections. The position also manages key functions of BarryConnect/12Twenty, supports career programming and employment outcomes reporting, job placement statistics and serves as a key operational partner to the Director of Career Services & Employer Relations. Employer Relations, Recruitment, Opportunity Development & Social Media Engagement Identify law firms, government agencies, courts, public interest organizations, corporations, alumni, and other employers to expand employment opportunities for students and alumni. Research, identify, invite, and follow up with prospective employers to expand On Campus Interviewing, resume collections, job postings, career fairs, and other recruiting opportunities. Market Barry Law students and alumni to employers in Central Florida and other strategic regional and national markets. Create, maintain, audit, and expand employer contacts database and recruiting records in BarryConnect/12Twenty. Support the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations with employer engagement, targeted outreach campaigns, and marketing materials that support recruitment and placement goals. Under the direction of the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations, create and manage social media content development and engagement for outlets such as Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn. Career Counseling & Student Professional Development Provide individual and group career counseling to assigned students, with primary responsibility for second year (2L) students, regarding career exploration, job-search strategy, networking, professional development, and employment preparation. Review resumes, cover letters, and other application materials; conduct mock interviews; and provide individualized feedback on interviewing, networking, and job-search techniques. Develop short- and long-term action plans with students and provide appropriate follow-up and accountability. Remain current on legal-market trends, recruiting practices, and applicable NALP guidance and translate relevant information into practical student advising. Collaborate with the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations to ensure continuity of career advising across the student lifecycle and refer complex or specialized matters to the Director appropriate. Pro Bono & Community Service Program Administration Identify and maintain approved legal and community organizations database to expand pro bono, public service, and community service opportunities for students. Maintain and routinely audit approved provider and opportunity databases and student-facing resource lists to ensure information is current, accurate, appropriately categorized, and accessible. Research and develop new opportunities consistent with School of Law requirements and departmental priorities. Coordinate updates with participating organizations and support student questions regarding available opportunities and established submission/approval processes. Assist with pro bono and public interest programming, fairs, outreach initiatives, and related communications. Recruitment Programs, Career Programming & Networking Events Supports the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations with professionalism programs that support students and alumni with career planning and job-search efforts. Coordinate with the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations to develop career-path, professionalism, and job-search programming for students and alumni, including private sector, public sector, judicial, public interest, and non-traditional career pathways. Under the direction of the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations, plan and execute On Campus Interviews, resume collection programs, career fairs, employer information sessions, panels, workshops, and networking events throughout the year. Coordinate program logistics, communications, employer participation, student preparation, and post-event follow-up. Evaluate programming and recruiting initiatives and recommend improvements based on participation, outcomes, and stakeholder feedback. Identify off-campus and community-based networking opportunities that strengthen employer and alumni relationships. Research and identify student professional development opportunities BarryConnect/12Twenty & Career Services Systems Administration Manage assigned daily functions of BarryConnect/12Twenty and serve as a departmental point of contact for system operations and vendor support. Maintain job database and process employer registrations, job postings, on-campus interview sessions, resume collections, and related recruiting workflows. Promote BarryConnect/12Twenty to students, alumni, and employers and support effective user adoption. Remain current on platform features and changes; assist with staff training, documentation, data integrity, and continuous process improvement. Support approved digital communications and project-management tools used by Career Services. Data, Reporting & Employment Outcomes Assist the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations with maintaining data integrity across Career Services systems and records. Support employment outcomes reporting, including at-graduation and 9-month post-graduation surveys and related reconciliation activities. Compile and analyze program, employer, student engagement, and placement data to inform departmental planning and continuous improvement. In collaboration with the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations, coordinate and review assigned work of student office assistants and/or student employees in support of Career Services priorities. Maintain organized operational records, templates, Standard Operating Procedures, and shared departmental resources for assigned areas. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations in support of departmental and School of Law priorities. Department Operations & Other Duties In collaboration with the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations, coordinate and review assigned work of student office assistants and/or student employees in support of Career Services priorities. Maintain organized operational records, templates, Standard Operating Procedures, and shared departmental resources for assigned areas. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the Director of Career Services and Employer Relations in support of departmental and School of Law priorities. Qualifications & Requirements: Bachelor's Degree Required – Field of study: Business Administration, Communications, Human Resources, Counseling, Legal Studies, or a closely related field. (Preferred) Master's Degree - preferred Field of study: Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, or another closely related field. (Preferred) 3-5 years previous experience Relevant experience in student affairs, career services, employer relations, recruiting/talent acquisition, workforce development, student professional development, higher education, legal recruiting, or a closely related field strongly preferred . Previous advising, coaching, teaching, guidance, or counseling experience preferred. Previous higher education experience preferred. A J.D. is not required. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-Physician-Assistant-Program_R0007911": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Medical Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nSummary Barry University’s College of Health Professions and Medical Sciences (CHPMS) is seeking a dynamic and innovative full time (12 month) faculty member to join our interdisciplinary group of healthcare experts. This position will be dedicated to our graduate-level Physician Assistant program (Master of Clinical Medical Sciences). This position is In-Person Essential Functions Teach graduate-level courses in the physician assistant program. Provide student mentorship and advising, including master’s thesis/projects. Engage in Program, College, and University service. Engage in scholarship. Qualifications/Requirements Graduate of an accredited physician assistant program or accredited allopathic/osteopathic medical program. Current, unrestricted Florida licensure as a PA, medical or osteopathic physician, or eligibility. Current NCCPA or physician board certification or eligibility. Master’s degree required. An earned doctorate in a health-related field or in education preferred. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience. Prior faculty experience is preferred.  Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Financial-Aid-Processor_R0007922": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Processor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nSummary The Financial Aid Processor position handles all financial aid processing tasks, including but not limited to: ISIR import/export, loan origination, import/export and processing, file verification, reporting, document review and tracking, awarding, crediting Title IV funds, and other non-counseling financial aid tasks. Essential Functions Performs all functions related to student loan origination and disbursement management: • Identifies loans that are ready for origination, marks files, and exports loan data electronically to the Common Origination & Disbursement (COD) platform using Colleague • Imports loan responses from COD and corrects and resolves all rejected response records • Monitors the electronic import of required loan documents from COD, such as the Master Promissory Note and Loan Entrance Counseling • Processes loan cancellations and reductions, and works with CBO to ensure reversal of funds and that corrected information is exported to COD • Performs daily loan disbursement process, including creating disbursement saved list for CBO and then exporting disbursement information to COD • Works jointly with Quality Control Supervisor on resolving system issues, updating records, and creating loan reports. • Oversees process for Parent PLUS loans, including data entry and export, monitoring credit decisions, and sending communications to parents/students. Completes ISIR file verification in accordance with federal Title IV guidelines: •Compares parent/student federal tax data to ISIR income/asset data for accuracy, making corrections when necessary, and electronically exports information to the Department of Education • Ensures daily import/export files in Colleague and Student Financial Success Form •Generates verification status reports for review. • Maintains 100% verification file review compliance and has working knowledge of federal tax filing requirements, specifically IRS Publication 17 • Ensures compliance with laws and regulations regarding federal and state regulations and school policies and procedures. Performs routine daily processing and office tasks: • Requests additional information on the Student Financial Success Form to resolve conflicting information • Ensures that correct missing document requests are added to the student record • Oversees office mail collection (both internal and external), delivery to the mail room, and distribution • Maintains responsibility for student file creation and ongoing management • Oversees office supply orders and inventory. Crediting PELL Grant and SEOG • Credits PELL and SEOG in accordance with federal/state regulations • Ensures PELL/SEOG disbursements are reconciled with Colleague and COD • Assists with reconciliation and reporting to COD. • Adjusts PELL/SEOG amounts before crediting. • Exports corrections to COD when student changes registered credits and affects aid eligibility. Review and resolve ISIR critical comment codes • Perform data analysis to identify discrepancies in data and determine action for resolution • Ensure to identify different federal documents (e.g., domestic/foreign passports, forms I-551, I-94, status information letters) and know which documents are appropriate for clearance • Runs secondary verification process when eligible non-citizen status is undetermined. Checks the SAVE System DHS • Ensures clearing SAR C-Flags for verification, direct loan rejects, resolution of conflicting information, certifying PLUS/GRAD Direct Loan applications, award revisions, and rejected disbursements. Performs all functions related to reporting • Ensure reporting processes in accordance with federal regulations • Review and report results on a weekly basis to NSLDs for Transfer Monitoring • Ensure monthly reporting to FAA access to report V4/V5 results • Maintain detailed records of import/export files. Perform awarding processes • Review and identify students that are ready to be awarded • Award new students with a valid admissions status and ISIR with no C-codes • Award returning students with valid ISIR, no C-codes • Ensure all C-flags and rejects have been resolved before awarding students • Verify completion of Master Promissory Note and Loan Entrance Counseling Perform other miscellaneous duties as assigned • Maintain current knowledge of financial aid federal, state, and school regulations • Read, understand, and comply with federal, state, and school policies and procedures • Respond to communication (email/voicemail) daily. • Liaison to and provide support to the Financial Aid Counselors, internal departments, and external organizations; answer questions, inquiries, or requests regarding processing and disbursing loans and crediting PELL/SEOG. Perform processing tasks on various platforms • Daily use Colleague to perform all processing duties • Daily use Student Financial Success Form to maintain and process student documents • Run daily/weekly reports using Entrinsik Informer Report • Utilize federal websites, such as COD, FPS Access, NSLDS, etc., to keep current on federal/state regulations and processing. Qualifications/Requirements A high school diploma is required. An Associate's degree is preferred. 1-3 years of relevant experience. Intermediate experience with CRM is required. Must be able to work independently and apply financial aid concepts to a variety of situations. Must have strong written/oral communication skills to communicate clearly and professionally with internal and external stakeholders. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Pembroke-Pines---Pines-Blvd/Adjunct-Instructor--High-School-EMT_R0007923-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, High School EMT",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\nThe High School EMT Instructor is responsible for delivering high-quality EMT instruction to high school students enrolled in this specialized high school program. This position ensures that students gain the necessary knowledge and skills to meet state and national EMT certification requirements. The instructor follows established curriculum guidelines, maintains compliance with accreditation standards, and supports student success through mentorship and hands-on training. This role requires collaboration with the High School Program Coordinator, the High School faculty, and clinical partners to create a comprehensive learning environment All Barry EMS (EMT and Paramedic) Instructors ensures that course delivery adheres to Florida BEMS 64J standards and NATIONAL STANDARDS EMT and Paramedic Scope of Practice . EMT Instructors shall maintain accurate records of student attendance, progress, and certification eligibility in compliance with program policies.  Instructors be well versed in the delivery of EMT course content with the end goal of properly preparing students for NREMT licensure examination The High School EMT Instructor is the primary person who I responsible for preparing students for emergency service entry point.  This position requires strong leadership, adaptability, and enthusiasm for EMS education. Instructors works closely with the High School Program Coordinator, and industry professionals to ensure students are fully equipped with the knowledge required to succeed in their EMT careers. Instruction and Classroom Management: Deliver EMT course instruction aligned with state and national standards, utilizing both classroom-based and hands-on training methods. Foster an engaging and supportive learning environment while ensuring students develop competency in essential EMT skills and knowledge. Maintain classroom discipline and encourage student participation. Clinical and Lab Training: Oversee and facilitate practical skill labs and simulations, ensuring students develop proficiency in patient assessment, life-saving interventions, and pre-hospital emergency care. Monitor and evaluate student performance during hands-on exercises.20 Student Assessment and Evaluation: Develop and administer quizzes, exams, and practical skill evaluations to assess student progress. Provide constructive feedback and additional instruction as needed to ensure student comprehension and skill mastery.  Be accountable for final student test scores and student NREMT certification. Compliance and Accreditation Support: Maintain accurate records of student attendance, progress, and certification eligibility in compliance with program policies. Student Mentorship and Support: Serve as a mentor and resource for students, providing guidance on academic success, career pathways, and professional development. Address student concerns and collaborate with the Program Coordinator to support student retention and success. Equipment and Inventory Management: Assist in maintaining lab equipment and training materials, ensuring resources are available and in good condition for instructional use. Report equipment needs to the Program Coordinator for timely replenishment. Requirements: Associate Degree, or vocational or technical school degree Valid Drivers License Paramedic License and ACLS Instructor 1-3 years precious experience Working knowledge of Microsoft Office software Excellent written and verbal communication skills Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Associate-Dean-of-Clinical-Affairs-and-Community-Engagement--School-of-Podiatric-Medicine_R0007920": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of Clinical Affairs and Community Engagement, School of Podiatric Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nSummary The Associate Dean of Clinical Affairs and Community Engagement  provides strategic leadership, oversight, and operational management of all clinical programs within the School of Podiatric Medicine. This role ensures excellence in clinical education, supervises clinical faculty, maintains accreditation compliance for clinical training, and develops robust community partnerships to enhance student learning, outreach, and service opportunities. The position also leads initiatives that expand the school’s regional presence, strengthen external affiliations, and advance community engagement as an integral part of the podiatric medical curriculum. Working Relationships: Reports directly to the Dean. Works collaboratively with the Associate Dean of Academic and Student Affairs, clinical faculty, staff, and external community partners. Represents the school to hospitals, clinics, professional organizations, and community groups. This position is In-Person Essential Functions Clinical Functions – Clinical Education Oversight Plan, coordinate, facilitate, monitor, and assess the clinical education component of the curriculum in alignment with institutional and accreditation requirements. Develop and implement clinical curriculum components to ensure high-quality, contemporary training across various clinical settings. Collaborate with clinical faculty to assess and enhance the effectiveness of clinical education programs, including clinical clerkships and rotations. Maintain continuous communication with clinical education faculty, clinical sites, and preceptors to ensure consistency, quality, and support for student learning. Ensure compliance with all accreditation standards related to clinical training for students, faculty, and preceptors. Provide oversight of faculty and preceptors involved in clinical rotations and ensure operational coordination across all clinical education settings. Community Partnerships Build and maintain strong relationships with healthcare providers, clinics, hospitals, and community organizations to create robust educational and service-learning opportunities. Coordinate outreach programs that address community health needs and promote wellness initiatives. Serve as a liaison between the school and community stakeholders to strengthen collaboration and promote the school’s mission Student Engagement Facilitate student involvement in community service activities, outreach efforts, and clinical rotations to ensure a well-rounded and meaningful educational experience. Maintain ongoing communication with students regarding clinical training expectations, placement coordination, and performance feedback. Support, mentor, and guide students in their clinical development by offering resources, advice, and individualized support as needed. Program Development Identify opportunities to establish new clinical programs and initiatives that advance the school’s mission and address emerging community health challenges. Collaborate with faculty and staff to secure funding and resources required for community engagement projects and clinical program expansion. Innovate and expand clinical and community-based programs that enhance student learning, improve patient care, and strengthen institutional visibility. Research and Evaluation Encourage and support research initiatives focused on community health issues, clinical practice improvement, and educational outcomes. Collect, analyze, and evaluate data to measure the impact of community engagement initiatives and clinical programs. Prepare reports for internal and external stakeholders summarizing program effectiveness, student outcomes, community impact, and recommendations for improvement. Leadership and Administration Serve on committees and actively contribute to decision-making processes related to clinical affairs, curriculum development, accreditation, and community engagement. Prepare comprehensive reports and presentations on clinical education activities, student performance, partnerships, and community initiatives for the Dean, administrative leadership, and accrediting bodies. Provide administrative oversight to ensure the operational efficiency, strategic alignment, and continuous improvement of clinical and community engagement programs. Ensure consistent communication with faculty, staff, community partners, and students to support program integrity and responsiveness. Faculty Role and Collaboration Works closely with faculty members to enhance instructional strategies and integrate student feedback into the academic experience. Is a member of the faculty and engages in teaching courses in the school and practices medicine in the clinics. Represents the School of Podiatric Medicine and the Dean at internal and external meetings, professional organizations, university committees, and community functions. Participates in University committees and councils as recommended by the Dean. Collaborates with the Associate Dean of Academic and Student Affairs to support student success in clinical phases. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements Doctoral degree in Podiatric Medicine (DPM). Board certification in Podiatric Medicine and/or Podiatric Surgery, preferred. Academic rank of Assistant Professor (minimum)  and currently progressing toward promotion to Associate Professor; Associate Professor or higher preferred . Minimum of five years of experience in academic administration, clinical education, community health, or related areas.   Extensive clinical experience and understanding of podiatric medical education. Demonstrated understanding of contemporary podiatric medical practice, quality clinical education, the clinical community, and the healthcare delivery system. Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders including faculty, students, healthcare organizations, and community partners. Strong understanding of CPME accreditation standards. Commitment to student success, patient care quality, and community service. Preferred Prior leadership experience in a medical or health professional school related to clinical education or community engagement. Familiarity with current trends and challenges in community health, clinical training, and healthcare delivery systems. Proven track record of developing successful clinical programs and community partnerships. Scholarly activity or research in medical education, clinical practice improvement, community health, or related areas. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Director-of-Benefits-and-Wellness-Programs_R0007495": {
      "title": "Director of Compensation and Benefits",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nSummary The Director of Benefits/Wellness and Compensation provides strategic leadership, oversight, and administration of the University's employee benefits, wellness, retirement, leave, and compensation programs. The position partners closely with the Associate Vice President of Human Resources to develop, implement, and continuously improve HR policies, programs, and initiatives that support employee well-being, market competitiveness, internal equity, and regulatory compliance. The Director collaborates with University leadership and key stakeholders to evaluate positions, analyze compensation data, maintain salary structures, oversee salary surveys and IPEDS reporting, and recommend compensation strategies that align with the University's strategic goals and workforce objectives. Essential Functions Benefits and Wellness Program Leadership: • Establishes the strategic direction of the University’s benefits, wellness, retirement, leave, and insurance programs, including group health, dental, vision, life, LTD, workers’ compensation, retirement plans, tuition assistance, FMLA, leave plans, and 403(b)/401(k) hardship, loan, and withdrawal processes. • Evaluates and compares existing benefits and wellness programs with those of other institutions by analyzing plan design, benefit surveys, claims data, market trends, and other sources of information to recommend improvements or changes. • Develops annual goals, long-term objectives, annual action plans, policies, and procedures related to benefits, wellness, retirement, and leave programs. • Ensures University compliance with applicable federal and state laws and regulatory requirements related to benefits and wellness programs, including ERISA, health care reform requirements, COBRA, HIPAA, FMLA, IRS, Department of Labor, insurance commissioner, and other regulatory agency requirements. • Oversees required regulatory mailings, communications, reports, filings, and applications; serves as primary contact with third-party administrators, benefit providers, General Counsel, and external counsel regarding plan administration and compliance. • Analyzes aggregate health claims data to recommend and implement wellness initiatives designed to support employee wellbeing, lifestyle and behavior change, and long-term cost management. Compensation Program Administration: • Administers the compensation program for faculty and staff and works collaboratively with Talent Acquisition to determine offers for new employees that promote internal equity while remaining competitive with the external market. • Provides recommendations and guidance to managers on wages and salaries using the University’s Pay and Titling Guidelines, salary structures, external market surveys, and internal equity reviews. • Benchmarks positions against market surveys to determine appropriate market pricing and placement within salary ranges; completes exempt and non-exempt salary surveys, including AAUP and CUPA-HR, and develops techniques for compiling, preparing, validating, and presenting compensation data. • Approves compensation-related actions in Workday HCM; utilizes Workday reports to conduct analytics on wages and salaries; works with the HRIS Administrator to ensure compensation tables in Workday are updated to reflect minimum wage requirements, salary structure changes, and FLSA standards. • Keeps current on Workday compensation releases and uses Workday Community resources to stay informed on compensation functionality, best practices, and system implementation considerations. • Keeps apprised of federal, state, and local compensation laws and regulations to help ensure University compliance with wage and hour, minimum wage, salary basis, and related compensation requirements. Position Description, Job Evaluation, Classification, and Reporting: • Evaluates Position Description Questionnaires (PDQs) for new and existing positions to ensure duties and responsibilities, reporting structure, work experience, education, knowledge, skills, physical and working conditions, and University mission expectations are clearly defined. • Makes recommendations for PDQ revisions to support uniformity of job descriptions, job titles, and titling guidelines. • Investigates and analyzes position duties and responsibilities to determine appropriate FLSA classification, exemption status, job title, and salary range. • Conducts job analysis and desk audits; develops or revises PDQs/job descriptions when needed and determines appropriate salary grade levels. • Provides data to Institutional Research for the annual HR portion of the IPEDS report, including reviewing reports, conducting data validation, updating information, and serving as the Human Resources point of contact for the Institutional Research team. Compensation Projects, Salary Structures, and Policy Support: • Works collaboratively with the Associate Vice President of Human Resources on compensation-related projects, policies, procedures, and recommendations. • Conducts market research to monitor competitiveness of the University’s salary structures and recommends continuous improvement to compensation procedures and practices. • Proposes updates to salary structures that align with compensation trends and University objectives; assesses the associated costs of pay grade changes and reviews salary ranges/structures on a recurring cycle to support continued competitiveness. • Prepares compensation data reports, HR metrics, and analyses related to wages and salaries, including data needed for merit increases, cost-of-living adjustments, minimum wage adjustments, internal equity reviews, promotional adjustments, and other compensation actions. • Performs compensation project work including benchmarking pay practices, incentive pay, bonuses, and other wage and salary initiatives as assigned. Leadership, Committees, and Other Duties: • Provides oversight, and direction for Benefits and Compensation staff by establishing goals, assigning work, reviewing work quality, supporting productivity, conducting performance appraisals, and coaching when appropriate. • Develops, manages, and forecasts HR budgets related to benefits, wellness, and compensation. Prepares quarterly and annual reports relating to benefits, wellness, and compensation initiatives. • Serves on University and external committees as appropriate, including committees related to benefits, wellness, retirement, compensation, and HR advisory responsibilities. • Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements Bachelor's degree in business, Human Resource Management, or related field is required Master's degree in human resources management, or MBA preferred Certifications in CEbS, PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP is preferred. 5-8 years of previous compensation and benefits experience is required Advanced Analytical skills required Advanced written and oral communications skills required Must be able to analyze statistical data for claims, spend analysis for all benefit and wellness related programs Must be able to multitask and manage projects effectively Ability to utilize Microsoft Office applications (e.g., Outlook, Excel, Word, PowerPoint) and HRIS software (e.g., Ellucian, Workday, Softdocs etc.) Must have excellent interpersonal skills both written and verbal High customer service skills in relationship to consulting with supervisors and communicating with employees of Barry University.  Must have excellent proofreading and editing skills Must be able to communicate effectively as a presenter for benefit related meetings, workshops and training. Must possess excellent listening skills Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--School-Psychology_R0007918": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, School Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nPart time\n\nSummary Barry University’s Department of Counseling & School Psychology in the School of Mental Health provides a quality education in a caring environment for the adult student population. The Adjunct Faculty member will teach courses within the School Psychology master’s and specialist degree programs located on the main campus of Barry University in Miami. The School Psychology Program follows the scientist-practitioner model and is accredited by the National Association of School Psychologists and is approved by the Florida Department of Education. We are currently seeking adjunct faculty to add to our roster of contract faculty for assignments on an as-needed basis for the following Graduate Programs:           School Psychology (MS and SSP) Courses are delivered in several formats, including face-to-face and online; terms are seven (summer courses) and 16 weeks in length (fall and spring). Graduate courses meet once per week (Monday-Thursday) for three hours for the entire semester, with start times from 5:30 to 6:30. Adjuncts are responsible for consulting with their respective Program Directors in the development and execution of the course, as well as additional responsibilities outlined in the faculty handbook Qualifications/Requirements Minimum degree is a Specialist's degree in School Psychology; doctoral degree preferred. Applied experience in the field is required. Prior college-level teaching experience with an adult student population is preferred. Applicants should be comfortable using computer technology appropriate for graduate-level university courses and professional scoring platforms used by school psychologists. Please note – if teaching in any course that has remote sessions or if a course is designated as an online course – completion of Barry University’s Online Instructor training will be required. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Orlando--Law-Campus/Student-Ambassador--Marketing_R0007546-2": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador, Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nPart time\n\nPosition Summary The student in this position will provide assistance with duties related to marketing the School of Law to prospective students and the community. The Student Ambassador will assist and take direction from the  Associate Dean. Essential Functions Assist with marketing projects such as writing items to include in news stories, blogs, bios, website updates, and photography/video. Create content for social media platforms such as Instagram, TikTok, and more to include the following: on-campus photography, basic photo/video/audio editing, short form blogging, and file/media and task organization. Assist with law school marketing projects as they relate to prospective and incoming students (open house materials, orientation, admitted student events, etc.). Clerical duties as assigned by Associate Dean (filing, copying, and other duties as assigned). Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School of Law. Qualifications/Requirements Currently enrolled Barry University School of Law students in good academic standing. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Orlando--Law-Campus/Reference-Librarian---Assistant-Professor-of-Law-Library_R0007391": {
      "title": "Reference Librarian & Assistant Professor of Law Library",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nSummary The Reference Librarian & Assistant Professor of Law Library is responsible for the legal research instruction to all Barry Law students, teaching classes in the LLM and/or JD program, providing workshops, and instructing small groups and individuals on any topic of legal research. Additionally, this position assists law faculty with educational technology, scholarship submission and promotion, and identifying research materials. This position provides both traditional and virtual reference and research instructions to all library patrons to include students, faculty, staff, alumni, and members of the bar. The Reference Librarian & Assistant Professor is both an administrative and tenure track position. However, while on the tenure track, this position is not a member of the law school’s faculty. Essential Functions Provides reference and research assistance to library patrons: Consults with patrons in person or via telephone, email, or video conferencing Conducts reference interviews to determine the exact nature of the question Advises patrons about useful resources to answer the question Teaches the patron how to use the resources, if necessary Responsible for specific reference shifts as assigned by the Associate Director  Provides legal research and legal information literacy education to the Barry Law community: Conducts guest lectures in the first year Legal Research & Writing classes and other classes as requested by faculty Plans and creates research lessons using lib-guides, workshops, and video Provides one-on-one instruction to students and faculty Stays abreast of changes in legal technology Participates in Faculty Liaison Program: Serves as point-of-contact to the library for assigned faculty members Assists and instructs faculty members with the use of Canvas, video conferencing, and other instructional technology Consults with faculty members about scholarship agenda and necessary research resources and help locating materials Consults with and trains faculty Research Assistants Teaching: Teaches one or two graduate-level for-credit courses in the LLM and/or JD program  Databases and Artificial Intelligence: Develops instruction and programming focusing on artificial intelligence and legal technology that supports the Barry University School of Law Evaluates new artificial intelligence and legal technology products and services, recommends adoption of products and services, and serves as a local expert for faculty and students at the School of Law Institutional Repository/Faculty Scholarship: Trains each journal’s incoming editorial board on library resources and services Maintains the currency and accuracies of faculty scholarship uploaded to institutional repository Further develops new and innovative ways to promote faculty scholarship (i.e. library website, blogging, working with marketing) Works with faculty to assist with submitting scholarship for publication (i.e. Scholastica, SSRN, etc.) Other duties as assigned by the Dean of Law School, Law Library Director, Associate Director of Law Library, or Head of Technical Services. Requirements/Qualifications Both a Juris Doctor and an MLS degree are required. One to three (1-3) years of related experience required. This position requires a comprehensive knowledge of legal research and resources, expert skill level with Westlaw and Lexis, and an expert ability to learn and teach other legal information technologies, such as HeinOnline and ProQuest. Ability to consult with patrons, analyze advanced problems, and determine most appropriate resources to solve such problems. Ability to complete projects independently. High degree of proficiency in word processing, spreadsheets, power point, email, and database management. Ability to operate basic library equipment, such as computers, printer/copiers, and monitors. Ability to converse and correspond comfortably with highly educated students and faculty. Ability to demonstrate outstanding customer service skills when consulting with library patrons, including patience and friendliness. Ability to maintain calm when dealing with challenging patrons or situations. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Coordinator--School-of-Podiatric-Medicine_R0007863-1": {
      "title": "Admissions Coordinator, School of Podiatric Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nSummary The Admissions Coordinator plays a critical role in achieving BUSPM enrollment goals by ensuring smooth operations of all routine processes for developing and maintaining a positive relationship with podiatric prospects and applicants and providing overall support to the enrollment management operation for the School of Podiatric Medicine.  This position leads the admission file review process, oversees all applicant communication, coordinates all logistics for the interview process, including scheduling faculty, serves as the primary liaison to the AACPM, and, when necessary, represents BUSPM in all aspects of the operation in place of the Director.  Through these responsibilities, the Admissions Coordinator not only supports but actively contributes to the success of the enrollment management operation.  Essential Functions .   Admission file management and compliance operations Evaluate and score all applications according to our standard rubric, laying the groundwork for fair, consistent, and mission-aligned admission decisions. Monitor and track applicant progress through the admissions cycle, maintaining real-time updates across CAS, Colleague, and Salesforce to guarantee accuracy and transparency for both applicants and the admissions team. Manage and safeguard all applicant documents, including pre-interview materials, letters of recommendation, MCAT scores, and transcripts, ensuring completeness and compliance with AACPM standards, Admission requirements, and accreditation standards. Establish and maintain official student records in Etrieve, seamlessly and accurately transferring files from CAS and ensuring accurate record-keeping for all incoming students. Update and resolve student record issues in Colleague related to transfers, CAS integration discrepancies, Social Security ID requirements, and other critical data accuracy points. Create and organize the incoming class cohort in American DataBank, streamlining retrieval and compliance tracking for required background checks. Review and verify all background checks (FBI, drug screening, and criminal history) for incoming students to ensure institutional and regulatory compliance. Prepare longitudinal student analyses for the Academic Dean, delivering data-driven insights that inform academic planning, retention strategies, and institutional reporting. 2.   Prospect engagement and admissions communication management: Coordinate and send interview invitations to qualified applicants via CAS or university email, ensuring accuracy and professionalism in all outreach. Manage applicant correspondence through CAS, including admission decisions, scholarship notifications, and status updates, to provide timely and transparent communication. Support the Admissions Director with interview scheduling, including preparing invitations and confirmations, to ensure a seamless and positive candidate experience. Acknowledge and update applicant status upon deposit receipt, reinforcing engagement and securing enrollment commitments. Provide individualized admissions counseling to prospective students via email and phone, offering clear guidance on requirements, timelines, and opportunities within the program. Maintain consistent communication with applicants throughout the process, addressing questions and ensuring they feel informed and supported at every stage. Host campus tours and deliver program presentations, both virtually and in person, to prospective students and their families, serving as a key representative of the School. Guide incoming students through compliance requirements, including background checks and screenings, and liaise with American DataBank to resolve any issues efficiently. .   Interview coordination and candidate experience Collaborate with the Admissions Director to develop interview schedules each semester, coordinating virtual and on-campus sessions to optimize faculty and student participation. Assist the Admissions Director with managing the interview scheduling system (Schedule Once) Coordinate faculty participation by sending invitations and calendar requests to pre-clinical and clinical faculty and maintain accurate records of their scheduled interview sessions each semester. Oversee all on-site interview logistics, including coordination for welcoming interviewees, interviewee clinic visits, and dining arrangements, to ensure a seamless and welcoming experience. Schedule current students to participate on interview days for student group sessions virtually or on campus. Host additional guests accompanying interviewees, providing tailored information sessions or campus tours to further showcase the school, answer guest questions, and strengthen engagement. Serve as acting representative of the Admissions Director when needed, conducting interviews and engaging with prospective students to ensure continuity and maintain a professional, high-quality candidate experience, both on campus and virtually, providing comprehensive program overviews including financial aid, housing, campus tours, clinical experiences, and overall student life, ensuring a positive and professional candidate experience. .    Admissions operations and strategic support Act as the Admissions Director’s representative in their absence, attending meetings, presentations, and other official functions to maintain continuity and leadership. Travel nationally and participate in recruitment events to support both short- and long-term enrollment goals, representing BUSPM professionally to prospective students and partner organizations. Engage in virtual recruitment events, ensuring consistent outreach and maintaining the school’s visibility among prospective applicants. Coordinate marketing and promotional materials in collaboration with the Department of Brand Marketing and Communications, ensuring timely availability and alignment with recruitment initiatives. Plan and coordinate all aspects of new student orientation for incoming classes, including scheduling, coordinating invitations to and managing on-campus personnel (e.g., President, Provost, Dean, Student Support Services), and organizing guest speakers from professional organizations such as the Florida Podiatric Medical Association. Collaborate with student organizations such as the Florida Podiatric Medical Student Association to integrate their programming with official orientation activities. Manage catering and logistics for orientation events, coordinating with campus or approved external caterers to provide a seamless and professional experience. Prepare comprehensive orientation materials, including agendas and informational packets, to support a smooth onboarding process for new students. Oversee office procurement, including processing purchase orders and supplier invoices through Workday, ensuring fiscal accountability and operational efficiency. Support data-driven decision-making by generating, maintaining, and providing student data reports and fulfilling data requests from school administration. Extended scope of work Serve on the School Admissions Officers Committee of the American Association of Colleges of Podiatric Medicine (AACPM) and act as a voting representative for BUSPM when engaged in Committee work.  Travel biannually to attend meetings with the AACPM. Travel biannually to attend AACPM SAO meetings, representing BUSPM’s and the profession’s strategic interests. Provide regular AACPM applicant data reports for internal analysis while ensuring strict adherence to confidentiality standards. 5.   Extended scope of work Serve on the School Admissions Officers Committee of the American Association of Colleges of Podiatric Medicine (AACPM) and act as a voting representative for BUSPM when engaged in Committee work.  Travel biannually to attend meetings with the AACPM. Travel biannually to attend AACPM SAO meetings, representing BUSPM’s and the profession’s strategic interests. Provide regular AACPM applicant data reports for internal analysis while ensuring strict adherence to confidentiality standards. Collaborate with the Admissions Director annually to oversee Centralized Application Service (CAS) configuration and process improvements. Support major BUSPM events, including Commencement, Rite of Passage, and other signature programs—through planning and execution. Recruit, hire, train, supervise, and evaluate the Admissions Work Study staff, ensuring effective support for office operations. Serve as an active voting member of the BUSPM Admissions Committee, contributing to applicant evaluations and admissions decisions.  This includes scheduling all BUSPM Admissions Committee meetings. Participate in the BUSPM Academic Calendar Committee, providing input on academic scheduling and alignment with admissions processes and timelines. Maintain membership in the National Association of Advisors for the Health Professions (NAAHP) and travel to regional and national meetings to promote BUSPM’s programs. Qualifications/Requirements A Bachelor's degree in any discipline is required. 1-3 years of Admissions experience.' Previous experience coordinating orientation, recruitment events, committee meetings, and interviews.   Event planning and execution. Must be proficient with MS Office Suite, CA Colleague, and Salesforce. Strong time management skills; attention to detail; handling confidential documentation with discretion; functioning in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal command of English; Spanish preferred as well. Strong interpersonal skills to engage with constituents. Public speaking and presentation skills.   Customer service orientation and responsiveness. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant-II--Physician-Assistant-Program_R0007428": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II, Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nThe Administrative Assistant II - Data and Admissions assists in coordinating the office operations of a PA site location. Provides support to the faculty, staff, instructors, and students of the PA Program.  This position assists in program data maintenance and the admissions process. Provides backup for administrative assistants in Miami and St Petersburg.  Works in a team environment. *Note: This position is In Person at the Main Campus Essential Functions Admissions -  Process applications- assist the Admissions Coordinator in Processes electronic CASPA applications from the website and conducts initial application evaluations for the qualification of admission Completes weekly batch application downloads from CASPA and uploads to the Colleague Analyzes and resolves batch application upload errors and or application ambiguities Performs electronic updates to contact information, application status, and restrictions within Colleague Enters data of applicant GPA, GRE scores, and coursework evaluation into the algorithm spreadsheet and Pipeline Report and miscellaneous ad hoc reports for periodic review by faculty   Integrate Admissions with other teams Trains and supports faculty and staff on current admissions processes and University policies related to eligibility and matriculation Criteria.  Troubleshoot online platforms (i.e., MyBarry Accounts, CASPA, Barry main website) Participates in planning initiatives to enhance current application platforms used in managing the admissions process Attends Admissions Team & Committee meetings when scheduled Attends Webinars and telephone conference calls quarterly Collaborates within the Department, University-wide, and External Events Collaborates and interacts with various University staff related to document sharing and deposit payments (transcripts, GRE, applications, checks). Program Data Maintenance Works closely with the Assessment and Compliance Specialist and the Assistant Program Director to assist with all aspects of ongoing and periodic self-study to maintain PA program accreditation by the ARC-PA. Maintain the PA program database, assisting in data entry.  Examples include: Maintains PA Program document libraries and permissions on SharePoint with regard to faculty, staff, and students. Manages faculty, staff, student, and alumni survey implementation, collection, and distribution. Develop final reports and distribute to faculty as directed. Implements surveys as needed. Coordinates and monitors graduate catalog entries with the PA program web page to ensure accuracy and congruence of information. Provides orientation and training for program personnel on data systems and products. Serves on PA program teams and committees and develop agendas, minutes and reports. Didactic and Clinical Activities: Maintains Learning Management System-  Checks LMS settings for student list, assessment timing, and merge sections.  Assists in constructing LMS, including course content, exams, and assignments. Post announcements to students Creates and maintains preliminary schedules. Serve as the primary (or secondary) person to update and edit schedules. Confirms office times and guest lecturers on all course syllabi. Confirms lecture times, communicates conflicts, and proposes new times. Review faculty syllabi for exam and lecture conflicts Confirm all exam/ quiz times and dates for all courses and input into the didactic schedule. Routinely informs students of schedule changes. Assists in printing/ formatting clinical skills exams, creates pairings of first and second-year students and Clinical Skills Exam schedules as directed in the syllabus.  Coordinates and schedules first-year students’ patient care visits. Assists the Physical Diagnosis (PD) lab course director with tasks including, but not limited to-scheduling lab instructors, proctors, and professional patients for all student labs  Monitors student flow/ attendance during labs Maintains equipment and supplies necessary to serve all office functionality. Organizes and maintains inventory for PD lab supplies Creates and track attendances (log absences, update attendance system, manage daily sign in sheets, generate attendance reports) Inputs clinical information into database(s) Assists faculty and staff in LMS. Performs basic administrative office work to assist the needs of faculty, staff and adjuncts. Proctor exams, supervising students in classroom via the Learning Management System (currently Canvas). Proctors students testing in a distraction-free environment per accommodations. Assists faculty to proctor exams, supervising students in the classroom via the Learning Management System (currently Canvas). Receives visitors Answers telephone, takes messages, and replies to questions in accordance with general instructions.  Transmit instructions or information to and from staff members. Assists with PA Program Events such as New Student and Clinical Orientation Composes meeting agendas and minutes, correspondence, type and revises forms, tables, handbooks, spreadsheets, flyers, etc.  Assists with faxing, filing, and sorting.         Mails packages, distributes mail. Compose correspondence and memos from brief verbal instructions or notes. Assist with the Planning and Coordinating of Program Events   New Student Orientation, Primary Care Review Conference, White Coat Ceremony, Annual retreat, Medical Spanish, Clinical Orientation, and Interprofessional education events. Facilitates Program-wide events.  Collaborates with PA, CNHS, University-wide, and external events. Reserves rooms, classrooms, and works with vendors for food or equipment Medical Compliance Liaison Serves as backup to Track student compliance with program requirements via a confidential database Facilitate local site operations Maintain the Calendar for the PA Program. May include submitting IAV work orders and coordination of IAV techs through DoIT or St. Petersburg College when necessary. Communicates with University Partnership Center, St. Petersburg College, National University of Health Sciences CNHS and Barry departments. Coordinates local community events involving  faculty and staff Liaison for and participation in local community-sponsored educational events promoting the university and the PA program.  Secures and prepares materials/information as needed for projects, reports, meetings, and presentations Orders office supplies, assists faculty when ordering medical supplies Manages the office facilities by acting as a liaison with facilities management Organizes and maintains inventory for PD lab supplies Qualifications/Requirements High School diploma or GED is required. An Associate's degree or Vocational/technical training is preferred. 1-3 years of relevant experience is required. Advanced experience with the MS Office suite, LMS, and databases within the program. Excellent communication skills, verbal and written. Great customer service skills Must be able to attend local community-sponsored educational events. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Hollywood-FL/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Biomedical-Sciences_R0007908-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nSummary The Biomedical Sciences (BMS) program is a master’s degree program that prepares graduate students for the rigors of medical, dental, and other biomedical professional degree programs. The BMS program is offered in two modalities: online live and face-to-face in person. Professors teach in person in the classroom with both in-person and fully online student attendees at the same time. The Biomedical Sciences program is seeking a full-time faculty member with the expertise and experience necessary to teach biomedical sciences courses equal to the rigor of those taught in medical schools. Examples of content areas are: Gross Anatomy, Human Physiology, Molecular Genetics, Pathophysiology, Forensic Pathology, Embryology, Microbiology (and others).    The ideal candidate will have the background knowledge and teaching experience to deliver the content at the expected level.   Full-time faculty in the BMS program are expected to contribute to Barry University in the areas of teaching, scholarship, and service. This position is Hybrid (in-Person/Remote) The anticipated start date for this position is January 1, 2027. Essential Functions The Assistant/Associate Professor of Biomedical Sciences will be expected to teach a variety of lecture and lab courses every semester (Fall, Spring, Summer) and at least one elective BMS course per year.  The position requires academic advising of 60-80 BMS graduate students as they progress through the program.  In addition, the faculty member is expected to participate in scholarship and research within their area of expertise, presenting and publishing on a regular basis.  All full-time faculty at Barry University are expected to serve the university by participating in university governance and sitting on university committees. Qualifications/Requirements The ideal candidate must hold a doctoral-level degree (Ph.D., M.D., D.O., or D.P.M.) in a field directly related to biomedical sciences and must be able to demonstrate the ability to lecture on and clearly communicate topics related to Gross Anatomy and Human Physiology.  Experience teaching Gross Anatomy and Human Physiology at the graduate level is preferred, but not required.  The candidate must be located in or be able to relocate to the South Florida area and is expected to be present to teach lectures in person at the BMS campus in Hollywood, Florida. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Associate-Director-of-Development_R0007461": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nDevelop and execute strategies to build a portfolio and manage a pipeline of 75-100 major and principal gift prospects with the capacity to make gifts of $50,000 or more annually. This includes plans that involve the effective stewardship of major and principal gift donors. Complete a minimum of 125 face-to-face or virtual visits annually to cultivate and solicit major and principal gifts from a portfolio of prospects and donors. Collaborate with senior administrators, deans, faculty, and volunteers to develop ideas that translate the University's fundraising priorities into gift proposals and to align them with the investment of major and principal gift prospects.  Utilize CRM database and related donor and alumni management databases to gather, record and properly store information about prospects and donors. Attend local fundraising events and association meetings to raise the public profile of Barry University and expand its network of capable prospects, as well as community partnerships . FL Driver’s License required Ensure a high level of stewardship for assigned individual, corporate and foundation donors, including, but not limited to, the submission of timely mid- and year-end reports and financials as appropriate, and maintaining detailed records of solicitation activities. Additional Information: Please describe as clearly and concisely as possible any additional information that would be important to fully understand the role, responsibilities, nature and scope of the position. Work closely with the Associate Vice President for Development to ensure seamless efforts to support University’s highest needs. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and 3-5 years of relevant experience. Previous proposal writing experience. Advanced written and oral communications skills. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Counseling_R0007831": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nSummary The Counseling Program holds CACREP accreditation in its Master’s in Counseling with specializations in Marriage, Couple and Family Counseling; Clinical Mental Health Counseling; and School Counseling, as well as in its Ph.D. in Counseling. The Ph.D. in Counseling has a Marriage, Couple, and Family Counseling specialization. This nine-month faculty position encompasses responsibilities in teaching, research and scholarship, student clinical supervision, service, and academic advising within the Master’s and Doctoral programs. A Level II background screening is required for this position. If the candidate has completed a Level II screening within the past five years, the record may be retrieved with the candidate’s written consent. Essential Functions Teach 6 courses per academic year in the Master’s and/or the Doctoral Program in Counseling across all specializations and at the Miami Shores campus. Provide Academic advising to both Master’s and Doctoral level students Serve as chair, methodology and design, and/or committee member of doctoral dissertations. Serve in program, school, and university committees. Be involved in the counseling profession at the local, state, regional, national, and/or international levels Maintain ongoing research, scholarship, and professional development. Establish and maintain community relations. Support the counseling program in other duties as determined by program administrators. Qualifications/Requirements The candidate must have a Ph.D. degree from a CACREP-accredited program and have teaching experience in a counseling program. * Preference will be given to candidates who have: A Florida license (LMHC or LMFT) or are eligible for licensure. Certification in school counseling, and Clinical experience in school counseling, clinical mental health counseling, and/or marriage and family counseling. Level II screening Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Accessibility-Accommodations-Coordinator_R0007877": {
      "title": "Accessibility Accommodations Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nSummary The Accessibility Accommodations coordinator is responsible for coordinating the delivery of services for students registered with the Office of Accessibility Services (OAS), ensuring that all their approved accommodations are met. The Coordinator collaborates with the Federal Work Studies assigned to the Office in the delivery and proctoring of all accommodated tests and quizzes. The Coordinator is also in charge of assisting the Director in the day-to-day operations of the Office. This position is in-person Essential Functions Coordinates the processing, scheduling, proctoring, and delivering of accommodated tests for students registered with the Office of Accessibility Services, in collaboration with the Director and any Federal Work Studies assigned to the Office. Supports the Director in processing new student requests; sets up intake appointments; and maintains and updates individual confidential student records consisting of medical, psychological, and educational documents related to students’ specific disabilities and accommodation requirements. Assists the Director in monitoring the delivery of accommodations for students registered with the Office of Accessibility Services, including but not limited to creating Accommodation Memorandums for Faculty and Housing and procuring note-taking solutions, assistive technology (AT) solutions, and American Sign Language Interpreters. Responsible for managing the Office of Accessibility Services in the absence of the Director. Requirements/Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in any field required. 1-3 years of related experience. Must have excellent written and oral communication skills. A bility to collect and analyze information, problem-solve, and make decisions. Must be proficient in Microsoft Suite: Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Must have front desk experience and excellent customer service and telephone etiquette. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Simulation-Operations-Specialist_R0007880": {
      "title": "Simulation Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nSummary The Simulation Operations Specialist supports the technical preparation and execution of Simulation activities delivered in the Simulation Learning Center + Annex including course prep, cleaning, maintenance, and repair of SLC simulation and other media equipment. This position is In-Person ** This position requires some weekends and evenings. ** Essential Functions Operate the simulator during sessions and other computer-based multimedia systems and their components, including operation of video cameras, A/V, projectors, and other equipment. Assist faculty and students with different simulator technologies and resolve technical issues. Play the standardized patient as needed during simulation scenarios. Serve as simulator operator running pre-programmed scenarios with faculty instructor, assuring all equipment is set up for course programs. Understand the use and operation of different simulator technology. Research available technology and new resources to better assist students with simulation and practices. Follow standard operating procedures, instructions, and checklists to prepare, set up, and clean up simulation and procedural skills events.   Independently set up skills and stock simulation labs with needed supplies and equipment for simulation/educational sessions. Pre- and post-cleaning of equipment and used areas. Organize equipment in proper areas after each use. Participate in systems and procedures development. Participate in curriculum design meetings to facilitate technical planning and delivery for simulation activities. Work with instructors and facilitators on case development, testing, and running scenarios. Perform post-simulation activities, including operating the following: Video Cameras/iPads: Manage recording, playback, storage, and cataloguing of simulations. Debriefing Software Other technology related to simulation. Participate in the ordering and maintenance of supplies, materials, and equipment of SLC. Maintain inventory of supplies and equipment and conduct routine inventory updates. Provide recommendations for budgeting and purchase of equipment, supplies and materials. Conduct ongoing maintenance of all simulation equipment, including cleaning, repairing, and ensuring that all equipment is always maintained in good working order. Interface with program manufacturers regarding equipment troubleshooting and systems problems, as well as periodic upgrades.   Maintain records of maintenance and repairs required and completed. Participate in orders and requisitions through Workday. Interface with equipment manufacturers regarding equipment troubleshooting and system issues. Maintain current knowledge of simulation equipment catalogs and operation manuals. Participate in technical training as necessary. Communicate and collaborate effectively with faculty to achieve learning outcomes for SLC simulation. Provide technical assistance, support, and training to faculty, instructors, students, and staff in the use of simulation equipment, as necessary. Generate innovative approaches for technology improvement and integration into healthcare education. Maintains SLC calendar through SharePoint & SLC Bulletin board. Maintain track of upcoming events and simulations. Provide administrative support to ensure smooth daily operation of the simulation-learning center. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements An Associate’s degree, or vocational or technical school degree – Field of Sciences/Nursing/Computer Science/Psychology/Instructional Technology/Communications Technology is required. A Bachelor's degree is preferred. 1-3 years of pr evious experience in healthcare simulation. Must be available some weekends/evenings as required. Ability to operate and troubleshoot Laerdal & Gaumard-powered technology & other simulators Advanced experience with Laerdal and Gaumard simulators and task trainers. Excellent written and oral communication. Excellent interpersonal skills. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---School-of-Business-and-Public-Administration_R0007875": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - School of Business and Public Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nPart time\n\nSummary The D. Inez Andreas School of Business and Public Administration (ASBPA) offers Bachelor's and Master's degree programs in various areas of business. The School emphasizes developing ethical business leaders who are socially responsible, have an entrepreneurial attitude, and a global perspective. The programs are accredited by AACSB-International, which speaks to the quality of the programs and the School`s processes. Essential Functions Teach undergraduate courses in Accounting and Business Statistics. Courses are offered during daytime hours, via in-person in-classroom lectures, on the Miami Shores campus. Qualifications/Requirements Master’s level in discipline, PhD preferred. Prior experience with university teaching in a face-to-face setting is also preferred. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Score-Table-Event-Technician_R0007871": {
      "title": "Score Table Event Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\nSummary This position is responsible for assisting the Barry Sports Information office staff in event score table activities during scheduled home games including score book/score sheet, scoreboard, and shot clock. This is an In-Person position Essential Functions Assist with setup for athletic events, including soccer, volleyball, basketball, baseball, tennis, golf, softball, and rowing. Provide support during athletic events operating scoreboard, videoboard, assisting with internet broadcasts as well as other game day activities. This also includes statistics, a shot clock, scorebook. Assist with tickets and concessions at various athletic-related events. Support marketing and social media efforts for athletic-related events. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements High school diploma required. Bachelor's degree in Sport Management preferred. A valid driver's license is required. Experienced operating digital equipment and score book/score sheet preferred. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---Physics_R0007860": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\nPart time\n\nSummary To teach physics courses (lecture, supplemental instructions, laboratory sessions) and to collaborate with other faculty within and outside of the department in the development and execution of courses. This position is In Person. Essential Functions Teach physics lecture, supplemental instruction, and/or laboratory. Administer, proctor, and grade assignments. Follow the designated curriculum. Report grades in the Canvas Learning Management System and Student Planning. Comply with the laboratory safety guidelines. Responsible for collaborating with respective academic coordinators in the development and execution of the course as well as additional responsibilities outlined in the faculty handbook. Qualifications/Requirements A Master's degree in Physics is required. A PhD is preferred. Prior teaching experience is preferred. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---Physics_R0007856": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\nPart time\n\nSummary To teach physics courses (lecture, supplemental instructions, laboratory sessions) and to collaborate with other faculty within and outside of the department in the development and execution of courses. This position is In Person. Essential Functions Teach physics lecture, supplemental instruction, and/or laboratory. Administer, proctor, and grade assignments. Follow the designated curriculum. Report grades in the Canvas Learning Management System and Student Planning. Comply with the laboratory safety guidelines. Responsible for collaborating with respective academic coordinators in the development and execution of the course as well as additional responsibilities outlined in the faculty handbook. Qualifications/Requirements A Master's degree in Physics is required. A PhD is preferred. Prior teaching experience is preferred. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
