    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Hollywood-FL/Adjunct-Faculty--Epidemiology_R0006554": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Epidemiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-07-18\nPart time\n\nBarry University’s Biomedical Sciences (BMS) Master of Science Program in the College of Health and Wellness is currently seeking an individual who will teach Epidemiology at the graduate level to students in the BMS degree program. The BMS Epidemiology course is offered in a HyFlex format. The faculty member teaches the class as scheduled from a classroom at the BMS Hollywood campus while simultaneously teaching to online students who are synchronously logged in through MS Teams to participate with the classroom lecture. The adjunct faculty member will collaborate with other faculty within and outside of the department in the development and execution of this course. Steeped in a tradition of rigor, the BMS program prepare students who wish to advance as health care professionals or biomedical scientists. The BMS curriculum serves to strengthen a student’s application for medical, dental or other professional health education by delivering a sequence of core science courses similar to the first-year of a medical, dental, podiatric, or other professional school curriculum in biomedical sciences. The program is designed to provide motivated students with an intensive and unique learning experience. Preparation of class materials to teach a graduate level course in Epidemiology to students in the BMS graduate program. Utilization of Canvas, Teams, and ExamSoft to manage and deliver the BMS Epidemiology course. Delivery of graduate level lectures and teaching in a HyFlex format. BMS Epidemiology is a 3-credit hour course that meets in a hybrid environment (online students attend synchronously) once a week for 3 hours. Assessment and grading of students enrolled in the Epidemiology course—submission of grades at the end of the semester Qualifications/Requirements - 1-3 years of experience - PhD in Biomedical Sciences or related field with pertinent specific training in or related to Epidemiology; OR MD/DO professional medical degree - Previous experience teaching pathology concepts - Advanced experience with the p reparation of lectures, assignments, and exam materials for teaching purposes Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Counseling---School-Psychology_R0007953": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Counseling & School Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nSummary The Department of Counseling & School Psychology seeks to recruit a diverse pool of individuals who would be interested in serving as part-time Adjunct Faculty. The Adjunct Faculty member will teach courses in the graduate programs at locations in Miami Shores, Off-Campus sites, and Online. Courses are delivered in several formats, including asynchronous/online, hybrid, and face-to-face. Essential Functions Courses are delivered in several formats, including asynchronous/online, hybrid, and face-to-face, and terms are seven, 10, and 16 weeks in length (depending on program). Class times vary but are generally 3 hours each week on weekdays or on Saturdays. Generally, graduate courses are offered 3 hours once a week (during th e evening). A djuncts are responsible for consulting with their respective Program Directors in the development and execution of the course, as well as additional responsibilities outlined in the faculty handbook. Qualifications/Requirements Master's degree required. Doctoral degree in a discipline of graduate teaching preferred for MS/EdS courses and required for PhD or EdD courses. Licensed Counselor (LMHC or MFT), master's degree in mental health required, doctoral degree preferred. Applied experience in the field is required. Prior college-level teaching experience with adult student population is preferred. Level II clearance is required. ** Please note: If teaching in a fully online modality, completion of Barry University’s Online Instructor training will be required. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Field-Advisor--School-of-Mental-Health---Social-Work_R0007952": {
      "title": "Field Advisor, School of Mental Health & Social Work",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nSummary The School of Mental Health & Social Work at Barry University is committed to advancing and protecting the human rights of all individuals, with an emphasis on those most marginalized, through teaching, research, advocacy, and practice rooted in social justice.   The School of Mental Health & Social Work Field Advisor complements and advances the essential functions of a liaison for social work students (BSW and MSW) and field agencies. The Field Advisor’s primary function is to support and guide students in their internship experience. The Field Advisor establishes a collaborative relationship with the Associate Director of Professional and Clinical Practice and the agency-based Clinical Educator. The Field Advisor position at Barry University requires someone who is committed to the development of our students as competent social workers, able to demonstrate clinical practice skills, leadership, quality, the quest for social and economic justice in local and global communities, and dedication to continuous professional growth and development.   Anticipated start date : 01/04/2027 Essential Functions Oversee the internship experience of students at the BSW and MSW level and provide ongoing support to the agencies, which include but are not limited to the following:   Attends all required Field Advisor Orientations and Seminars and student orientations. Anticipates a minimum of 5-10 hrs. of field-related work per week. Monitors the student’s performance in the practicum and provides consultation to the student and Clinical Educator when challenges arise in field placement. Conducts two field visits to each assigned student per semester. Conducts one group advising session for all assigned students per semester at the designated program site. Creates and maintains contact notes that reflect ongoing activities and interactions with students and clinical educators. Ensures familiarity with Field Education Website Content and Repository content on Clinical Education. Ensures the timely submission of all required documents and the upload of Field Visit Review Forms. Evaluates the quality of each placement based on the matriculation status of the student and required learning experiences . Acts as a representative of the School of Social Work in the articulation of the theoretical framework of curriculum and its link to internship experiences, ensuring the pedagogical principles for field education courses are supported by the agency, interpreting policies and procedures related to clinical education and student internships, and providing accurate information and instructions in completing all required documentation. Carefully reviews the Field Assessments and evaluations prior to submitting a recommended grade formFollows all established protocols for resolving issues in Clinical placementsReports any issues by mid-semester and/or as soon as possible to the Director of Professional and Clinical PracticeMakes recommendations of grades to the Director of Professional and Clinical Practice. Conduct two (2) (minimum 1-hour) agency site visits per semester to review the Learning Plan, student progress and final assessment. Conduct (at least one) group advising seminar on campus per semester to include; Reviewing the assigned advisee list sent by Office of Professional and Clinical Practice and posted in the repository in the One Drive site Ensuring that contact is established with the student on a weekly or bi-weekly basis for the duration of each semester Reviewing the Field Education Course Numbers and requirements under each course number and program (full or part-time), to include required hours, correct assessments, number of process recordings and field site visits per semester, Making an initial phone contact with both the Clinical Educator and the student at the start of each semester for the purpose of establishing a collaborative relationship with the Clinical Educator and Student and promoting a sound clinical learning experience Making sure all information pertaining to Clinical Educator contact information is accurate and reports any changes to the Associate Director of Professional and Clinical Practice for update. Creating an email group list for assigned Clinical Advisees to facilitate communication Completing a Field Education semester log to assist in overseeing that all clinical requirements are met by the end of the semester. Consults with the Director of Professional and Clinical Practice on all matters regarding students and clinical placement agencies Maintains ongoing and consistent communication with the Director of Professional and Clinical Practice Maintains ongoing contact with the Associate Directors of Professional and Clinical Practice at the Miami Shores site as initial points of contact and reference Seeks assistance from the Director of Professional and Clinical Practice on matters that may impact the student’s matriculation, including student attendance, progress in internship, potential incompletes in Clinical Education, Change of placement requests, Agency’s inability to meet the requirements for Field learning experiences, and Core performance issues. Qualifications/Requirements A Master's degree in Social Work is required. LCSW preferred. 1-3 years of relevant experience is required. Knowledge of and demonstrated application of social work practice skills in clinical intervention with individuals, families, groups, communities, and/or organizations.  Utilize the School's technology, e.g. Online student records, email, Canvas, in content delivery and communication with students, faculty, and staff. Strong verbal and written communication skills necessary to provide feedback to students regarding demonstration of competency A valid driver's license is required.   Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Physiology---School-of-Podiatric-Medicine_R0007951": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Physiology - School of Podiatric Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nSummary Barry University School of Podiatric Medicine, located in Miami Shores, FL, between Miami and Fort Lauderdale, invites applications from dynamic candidates for an adjunct faculty position to teach a four-credit Physiology I course in the spring 2027 semester ( January 4 through April 23, 2027). This position is In-Person. Essential Functions The primary responsibilities of adjunct faculty will be to teach this course in person. Administer and grade assessments utilizing ExamSoft™ testing system, report grades in the Canvas Learning Management System, proctor examinations in person, provide student advisement, and adhere to BUSPM protocols in the administration of the course. Qualifications/Requirements A PhD degree is preferred, although other appropriately well-qualified candidates may be considered. Previous experience teaching in this field in a professional medical school setting is preferred. A strong commitment to teaching a diverse population of medical students is highly sought. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled.   Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Risk-Management_R0007950": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Risk Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nSummary Barry University's School of Podiatric Medicine, located in Miami Shores, FL, between Miami and Fort Lauderdale, invites applications from dynamic candidates for an adjunct faculty position to teach a one-credit Risk Management course in the spring 2027 semester ( February 22 through April 12, 2027 ). Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. This position is In-Person. Essential Functions The primary responsibilities of adjunct faculty will be to teach in-person the medical and legal aspects of podiatric medical practice, e.g., malpractice, medical jurisprudence, and ethics. Administer and grade assessments utilizing ExamSoft™ testing system, report grades in the Canvas Learning Management System, proctor examinations in person, provide student advisement, and adhere to BUSPM protocols in the administration of the course. Qualifications/Requirements A DPM, MD, DO, or JD degree is required. Previous experience teaching in the field in a professional medical school setting. A strong commitment to teaching a diverse population of medical students is highly sought. Other appropriately well-qualified candidates may be considered. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Practice-Management---School-of-Podiatric-Medicine_R0007949-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Practice Management - School of Podiatric Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nSummary Barry University School of Podiatric Medicine, located in Miami Shores, FL, between Miami and Fort Lauderdale, invites applications from dynamic candidates for an adjunct faculty position to teach a one-credit Practice Management course in the spring 2027 semester (March 17 through April 21, 2027). Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Director--Family-Wellness---Strengthening-Program_R0007946": {
      "title": "Director, Family Wellness & Strengthening Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nSummary The Director of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program is integral to the mission CARE Center. The Director of the Family Wellness & Strengthening Program provides administrative and programmatic oversight of year-round family wellness and strengthening program activities that include parenting-child group sessions and trauma-informed counseling sessions. The Director is responsible for timely submission of program and financial reports (monthly, quarterly, interim, and final) to the CARE Center Director and to the program funder/s. The Director is responsible for training and supervision of program providers and Barry research graduates. The Director is also responsible for increasing and promoting Barry University’s CARE Center and Family Wellness & Strengthening Program resources to community partners and internal University departments. A Level II screening is required for this position This is a full-time, grant-funded, in-person position . Essential Functions Oversight Administrative and programmatic oversight of year-round program activities: Oversight and supervision of duties carried out by program providers, staff, volunteers, subcontractors, practicum and internship students, research graduates Develops and provides program training and orientation program providers, staff, volunteers, subcontractors, practicum and internship students, research graduates Coordinates off campus and on-campus Family Wellness & Strengthening Program activities and resources by working closely with external partners and internal university departments. Coordinates Family Wellness & Strengthening Program staff/volunteer meetings Responsible for financial and program reports: Maintains program budget and fiscal ledgers on expenses to ensure timely submission of budget reports to the funder. Works with Program Coordinator to ensure timely submission of monthly invoices from program subcontractors to the University’s Grant Finance Office through the University’s system (i.e., Workday) Works with Program Coordinator to ensure timely completion and submission of monthly, quarterly, interim, and final grant deliverable reports to ensure timely submission to the funder. Collaborates with the University’s Grants Sponsored Office and The Children’s Trust (funder) and various departments to ensure the completion of affiliation agreements and contracts. Prepares and provides the program CARE Center Director with monthly reports for sharing during university meetings (Clinic Oversight Committee, CARE Center Advisory Council, etc.) Responsible for increasing and promoting Barry University’s CARE Center and Family Wellness & Strengthening Program resources to community partners and internal University departments: Director of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program is a member of community partnerships and CARE Center subcommittees; attends meetings to promote CARE Center and Family Wellness & Strengthening Program resources; shares program goals, collaborative opportunities, and program accomplishments. Director of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program works closely with CARE Center director to seek funding opportunities to support Family Wellness & Strengthening Program and its activities. Director of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program participates in community events to increase awareness and resources to the community (Health & Resource Fair, The Children’s Trust Family Expo, Back to School Fairs, Parent School Open House, etc.) Meets with community partners to review program goals, objectives, and outcomes. Works closely with The Children’s Trust (TCT) and University Marketing department to ensure program has the most up-to-date promotional material (i.e., TCT logo, University Logo, and CARE Center logo) for promotion of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program on websites, newsletters, brochures, documents, etc. Qualifications/Requirements Bachelor’s degree required – Field of study: Psychology, Social Work, Business/Public Administration Master’s degree preferred – Field of study: Human Services Field, Psychology, Social Work, Mental Health, Family Therapy 3 - 5 years of relevant work experience required Level II clearance is required. Must be able to perform administrative and program management Develops and manages program budget and reconciles purchases and expenditures Writes program reports, conducts presentations to community and university departments The Director of the Family Wellness & Strengthening Program within the CARE Center seeks and builds partnerships with the University service areas and community to carry out its mission and goals. The responsibilities of the Director of Family Wellness & Strengthening Program increase as additional community partnerships and funding opportunities increase. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Swim-Coach--Part-Time_R0007980": {
      "title": "Assistant Swim Coach, Part Time",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nSummary The Part-Time Assistant Coach is responsible for assisting in the direction of all phases of a nationally competitive program in accordance with Barry University, the Sunshine State Conference, and NCAA DII regulations. Specifically, duties include recruiting, handling video exchange, and individual instruction/player improvement, coordinating community involvement, completing/submitting administrative and compliance documents, and other duties assigned by the head coach.    Essential Functions   Organizes, supervises, and conducts teaching sessions:   Assists the head coach with instructing/ teaching student-athletes in the rules, regulations, and techniques of the sport. Organizes and directs individual and small group practiceactivities/exercises as directed by the head coach. Assists the head coach with supervising student-athletes during practices and competition. Follows established procedures in the event of an athlete’s injury. Teaches assigned fundamentals and skills during practice and games. Assesses players’ skills and keeps the head coach informed of the athletic performance of students. Models professional behavior and maintains appropriate conduct towards players, officials, and spectators.   Establishes and maintains an organized recruiting system: Recruits academically qualified student-athletes who form a competitive squad and meet established academic goals and objectives of the department. Participates in community service activities. Interacts with the Associate AD/SWA, ICA Compliance Coordinator, Coordinator for Student-Athlete Success, and Faculty Athletic Representative on all matters of eligibility.   Performs administrative functions in support of the Intercollegiate Athletic program:   Cooperates with the athletic administration in the implementation of department policies Assists in the direction of the program within the scope of the Intercollegiate Athletics Program Maintains a representative level of performance in the conference that satisfies departmental goals and objectives. Consults with the Assistant Athletic Director of Compliance concerning institutional, conference, and NCAA regulations that will directly affect the program. Maintains adequate records. Assists in Management of his/her budget and assists in developing fundraising efforts for his/her sport. Works closely with Sport Performance, Marketing, Development, and Athletic Communications.      Manages student data, including admissions, financial aid, registration, and academic performance data. All such data are treated as confidential in accordance with federal, state, and university regulations. The Assistant Coach updates and maintains information on the Compliance Assistant program, Salesforce, Workday, and the ACS Athletics program.   Qualifications/Requirements A Bachelor's degree in any discipline is required. A Master's degree is preferred. 1-3 years of proven experience is required. Must have a valid driver's license. Adept at written and oral communication Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Medical-Education_R0007972": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Medical Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nSummary Barry University’s College of Health Promotions and Medical Sciences (CHPMS) is seeking a dynamic and innovative full-time (12-month) faculty member to join our interdisciplinary group of healthcare experts. This position will be dedicated to our graduate-level Physician Assistant program (Master of Clinical Medical Sciences). Essential Functions Teach graduate-level courses in the physician assistant program. Provide student mentorship and advising, including master’s theses/projects. Engage in Program, College, and University service. Engage in scholarship. Qualifications/Requirements Graduate of an accredited physician assistant program or accredited allopathic/osteopathic medical program. Current, unrestricted Florida licensure as a PA, medical or osteopathic physician, or eligibility. Current NCCPA or physician board certification or eligibility. Master’s degree required. An earned doctorate in a health-related field or in education preferred. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience. Prior faculty experience is preferred. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Medical-Education_R0007970": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Medical Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nSummary Barry University’s College of Health Promotions and Medical Sciences (CHPMS) is seeking a dynamic and innovative full-time (12-month) faculty member to join our interdisciplinary group of healthcare experts. This position will be dedicated to our graduate-level Physician Assistant program (Master of Clinical Medical Sciences). Essential Functions Teach graduate-level courses in the physician assistant program. Provide student mentorship and advising, including master’s theses/projects. Engage in Program, College, and University service. Engage in scholarship. Qualifications/Requirements Graduate of an accredited physician assistant program or accredited allopathic/osteopathic medical program. Current, unrestricted Florida licensure as a PA, medical or osteopathic physician, or eligibility. Current NCCPA or physician board certification or eligibility. Master’s degree required. An earned doctorate in a health-related field or in education preferred. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience. Prior faculty experience is preferred.   Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant-III--CASA_R0007969": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant III, CASA",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nSummary The Administrative Assistant III serves as the administrative operations coordinator for the Center for Academic Success and Advising (CASA), overseeing the operational systems and administrative processes that support the department's daily functioning. The position coordinates student employment administration, facilities and technology operations, departmental logistics, space utilization, resource management, and high-volume customer service while serving as a central liaison with multiple university departments. This position exercises considerable independent judgment in coordinating operational priorities to ensure efficient and uninterrupted departmental operations. The attitude, courtesy and helpfulness of this position sho uld support Barry University in its mission to foster individual and communal transformation where lea rning leads to knowledge and truth , reflection lead s to inform e d action, and a com mitment to social justice leads to collaborative service. This position is in-person Essential Functions Administrative Operations Coordinates day-to-day administrative operations to ensure efficient functioning of the department. Serves as primary point of contact for incoming visitors, students, faculty, staff, and university administrators, providing outstanding customer service and directing inquiries appropriately. Manages high-volume office traffic and ensures efficient front office operations. Processes departmental mail, packages, deliveries, and outgoing correspondence. Provides cross-coverage for the Administrative Assistant III during scheduled breaks and absences to ensure uninterrupted office operations. Student Employment Coordination Coordinates all administrative processes related to student employees, including Federal Work Study and other student assistant positions. Coordinates recruitment, hiring, onboarding, employment documentation, scheduling, payroll processes, and offboarding of student employees. Serves as departmental resource regarding student employment procedures and university policies. Maintains employment records and monitors compliance with institutional requirements. Technology Liaison Serves as departmental liaison with Information Technology. Coordinates technology requests including equipment purchases, computer deployments, software installations, account access, telephone services, printer support, and troubleshooting requests. Maintains inventory of departmental technology resources. Assists with technology setup for new employees and workspaces. Space and Resource Management Coordinates departmental room reservations and space utilization. Collaborates with Conference and Events to reserve meeting rooms and event spaces. Assists with scheduling and logistics for departmental meetings, trainings, workshops, and special events. Monitors shared spaces to ensure readiness for daily operations and programs. Event and Program Support Supports the Operations Manager with planning and logistical coordination for departmental events, workshops, orientations, trainings, and supplemental programming. Assists with event preparation including room setup, materials, technology coordination, catering requests, and post-event logistics. Coordinates operational details to ensure successful program implementation Facilities Coordination Serves as CASA's liaison with Facilities Management. Coordinates maintenance requests, work orders, furniture needs, repairs, office moves, signage, and building-related issues. Assists in maintaining safe, functional, and welcoming office spaces. Collaboration and Communication Collaborates with internal and external stakeholders including Human Resources, Information Technology, Facilities Management, Conference and Events, Financial Aid, Payroll, Purchasing, and other university departments. Maintains effective communication across departmental teams to support operational efficiency. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements The successful candidate: An Associate's degree or Bachelor's degree is preferred. 3-5 years of administrative experience. Must have the ability to anticipate and identify problems and evaluate potential solutions; take or recommend appropriate actions and determine which problems to handle independently and which to refer; follow up on problems and help bring about resolution; and choose wisely from available courses of action, recognizing the impact of decisions on results. E stablish priorities and work to complete tasks within specified timeframes, while balancing the responsibilities of day-to-day operations. Possess a working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Publisher, Outlook, and SharePoint and be willing to continuously enhance skills with these technologies, and others, as work-related assignments require; ability to select appropriate technology with which to complete tasks and projects Excellent organizational skills to: facilitate the storage and retrieval of data; use tools and technologies to expedite completion of, and perfect, the required end-products; maintain and update Learning Center scheduling systems; and maintain and update Learning Center records and databases in a timely manner. Excellent oral communication skills; ability to communicate effectively with current and prospective students, parents, staff, faculty, and administrators within and across the University on a daily basis; pleasant and welcoming tone and speaks clearly in person and over the telephone; communicates clearly via email; written communications are free of grammatical, mechanical, syntactical, and spelling errors. Possesses a general understanding of Learning Center programming and University learning and academic support services; is able to effectively communicate this information to others (e.g., students, prospective students and their families, university personnel) and to refer students to appropriate personnel as needed, to facilitate student success. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Library-Technician-Public-Services_R0007976": {
      "title": "Library Technician Public Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nSummary The Library Technician provides a wide range of services, primarily focused on library patrons’ experience, but also assisting with tasks across all library operations. The position is responsible for the circulation desk, maintaining the physical stacks, and guiding and training work-study students. They also assist with services such as course reserves; interlibrary loans; acquisitions processing; digitization; and the Library’s social media presence; amongst other activities, depending on the Library’s needs.  This is an evening/weekend In-Person position. Essential Functions Public Service Customer service skills to ensure high-quality services and assist with departmental operations. Circulates materials to patrons at the Barry University circulation desk. Answers directional, light reference, and informational questions, and refers reference and other queries to librarians as appropriate. Assists patrons with photocopying and printing, provides routine maintenance/cleaning of photocopy machines, and reports malfunctions. Assists patrons in the use of computer catalogs and indexes, and audio-visual equipment and collections; provides appropriate routine emergency and preventive maintenance, and reports malfunctions of equipment. Creates library displays, contributes to “Staff Recommendations”, designs library outreach materials (often collaborating with other staff), participates in library open house events, and contributes to social media outreach through library accounts. Performs all public service tasks in a friendly and efficient manner; contributes to a welcoming atmosphere for library patrons. Contributes to the organization and creation of processes to enhance library services. Designs and implements organizational projects as needed. Maintains effective methods of communication with faculty and students, circulation staff, and other library staff. Technological skills including performing Public Services tasks (performing circulation transactions, processing requests and traces, opening/ closing of the library, processing, and assisting reserve requests, assisting patron inquiries and issues) Collecting fees/ fines for library materials   Staffing the circulation desk ( responding to patron issues and questions regarding the library and its collection, assisting in solving patron technical issues regarding library-related equipment. Collection Maintenance Coordinates and participates in stack maintenance activities including shelving and shelf reading of all library materials, and assists in training and supervising student assistants in these areas.Processes claims-returned/not-on-shelf searches, following automated and manual procedures, and records related statistics.Maintains new periodicals and new bookshelf areas. Library Services Active attendance at departmental meetings as scheduled by the Public Services Manager. Active attendance at the monthly library team meeting. Assists Librarians with library processes. Assists the Library Director and Associate Director with library processes as needed. Processes donations following library procedures. Transferring and assigning library-related materials to designated areas and departments for repair, relocation, etc. Searching for and collecting misplaced items and returning them to their appropriate location for patron use. Assist in the daily flow of library operations by: Aiding with other units within the library when necessary, and assisting in gathering data for library reports and statistics. Providing patron assistance and displaying supportive customer service with all constituents of the university. Performing data input, and aiding in collaboration with library supervision regarding the usage of library resources, and statistical data for library-related reports. Assisting patrons with computer-related issues, and solving technical-related issues concerning the library, and its resources. Financial Management Collects fines and membership dues, and conducts other appropriate financial transactions at the circulation desk. Prepares deposits and ensures appropriate cash handling and security procedures as assigned. Contributes to maintenance of departmental supplies and timely preparation of supply orders. Assists in circulation desk contingency scheduling for staff absences. Attends Library Staff, Circulation Working Group, and various other meetings of standing and ad hoc library groups. Other duties as assigned Qualifications/Requirements An Associate's degree or vocational/technical school degree is required. A Bachelor's degree is preferred. Previous experience in the same or similar position. Must have the ability to direct, monitor, and evaluate workflow. Performs various operations, basic instruction and communication of the department, library, and university, answers & routes calls and other information to the appropriate persons, or campus departments. Use email and other communication software. Must be able to communicate effectively and professionally at all times. Must able to work evenings/weekends Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Coordinator-for-Programs-and-Outreach_R0007956-2": {
      "title": "Coordinator for Programs and Outreach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nSummary The Coordinator for Programs and Outreach plans and delivers programs supporting Barry University’s mission and the Health, Arts, and Spirituality (HAS) Initiative. Serving as a visible representative of HAS, the coordinator engages students, employees, and community members; collaborates with campus partners; promotes events; and supports the Initiative’s continued growth.   Essential Functions Plan and execute HAS programs for Barry University students in collaboration with campus partners. Foster community engagement and align programming with the HAS Initiative’s vision and Barry University’s mission and core commitments. Manage HAS social media and promote programs and events in coordination with Marketing and Brand. Represent HAS at university and community events, engaging students, employees, and external stakeholders. Collaborate with the HAS Director, the Executive Dean’s Office, and the HAS Graduate Assistant on Initiative priorities and assigned projects. Qualifications/Requirements Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in health, arts, spirituality, or a related field preferred. One to three years of relevant work experience. Strong program planning, project coordination, and event-execution skills. Effective written, verbal, interpersonal, and social-media communication skills. Ability to work on campus Monday through Friday, generally 9:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m., with some evening and occasional Saturday availability. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Graphic-Designer_R0007962": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nSummary To routinely create innovative, high-quality print and digital visual solutions for the marketing and communication needs of various clients that align with the brand standards and contribute to the team's creative excellence. Essential Functions A key member of the Barry Ad Company and Marketing and Brand department, the Graphic Designer develops and maintains creative assets for branding and marketing communications towards the goals of building enrollment, increasing retention, and enhancing visibility and reputation within the community. The graphic designer develops a wide range of creative solutions that are both traditional (print, collateral materials, on-site, OOH, etc.) as well as digital. Must show a high level of creativity and creative curiosity in developing graphic design concepts. Must have mastery in layout and production design using design apps (Adobe Creative Cloud) and/or others. Must have criteria for photo selection, retouching and image archiving. Must have knowledge of color theory and color relationships, typography terms and specifications, page composition and grid structure. Assists with providing accurate time and cost estimates for printing, proofing, and delivery. Manages projects. Works closely with marketing clients on deliverables. Maintains strict adherence to deadlines, deliverable specs, client briefs and feedback. Keeps up to date with software enhancements, design, and visual communication trends.  Organizes and maintains project files. Serves as a mentor and a guide for student ad company staff. Must be able to accept feedback and direction (that may vary from positive to negative), address revisions based on this feedback and post for continuing approvals.  Participates in the development of creative solutions to effectively communicate through a wide variety of creative tactics. Works with the Art Director, and the account service team to manage workflow of all projects, which includes the interaction with the Communications team, outside agencies, copywriters, and freelancers. Must be able to manage multiple projects simultaneously, and meet specified deadlines. Participates in weekly departmental staff meetings and any creative meetings. P rovide accurate time and cost estimates for deliverables, as assigned. Assists at photo/video shoots. Oversees the creative asset production process ensuring production techniques, and file accuracy. Meets established deadlines and posts work for approval on Workfront (or similar project management system). Other duties as assigned or as proactively identified.   Qualifications/Requirements Required: High school diploma or GED Required: Associate’s degree, or vocational or technical school degree – Field of study: Advertising, Communication Design or Visual Arts Preferred: Bachelor’s degree – Field of study: Advertising, Communication Design or Visual Arts Less than 12 months related experience required THIS ROLE IS FULL-TIME, ON-CAMPUS IN MIAMI SHORES. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    },
    "https://barryu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/BarryU/job/Miami-Shores--Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-Physician-Assistant-Program_R0007917": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nSummary Barry University’s College of Nursing and Health Sciences (CNHS) is seeking a dynamic and innovative full-time (12-month) faculty member to join our interdisciplinary group of healthcare experts. This position will be dedicated to our graduate-level Physician Assistant program (Master of Clinical Medical Sciences). This position is In-Person Essential Functions Teach graduate-level courses in the physician assistant program. Provide student mentorship and advising, including master’s theses/projects. Engage in Program, College, and University service. Engage in scholarship. Assist Program Leadership in coordinating clinical rotations. Qualifications/Requirements Graduate of an accredited physician assistant program or accredited allopathic/osteopathic medical program. Current NCCPA or physician board certification. Current, unrestricted Florida licensure as a PA, medical or osteopathic physician (or eligibility).   Master’s degree required. An earned doctorate in a health-related field or in education preferred. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience. Prior faculty experience is preferred. The College of Nursing and Health Sciences places high value on previous experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and experience using distance learning technology. Benefits: Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time employees that includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, tuition assistance, paid time off and work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace, and training and development. Barry University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a diverse and inclusive work environment."
    }
  },
